{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261123T193709Z-4cce97ff", "ts": "2026-11-23T19:40:50Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.9.1-dev", "branch": "fix/verify-links-review-id", "build": "ecd39ffbf786"}, "body": {"base_commit": "ecd39ffbf786afb8069915758108afe00603ddfa", "base_tree": "791cfefb6a97bd6b0e98fa5d718b0ec27734b512", "head_tree": "b3d841235d3f7b8e658cef196dad00368f075c4d", "head_commit": "f77538e195893badc370eeabc45a6b7284609108", "dispatch_commit": "f77538e195893badc370eeabc45a6b7284609108", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py", "plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/lib/plan_status.py", "plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md", "tests/test_critic_gate_fallthrough.py", "tests/test_session_critic_gate.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py", "tests/test_verify_links_review_id.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/verify-links-review-id.md", "plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py", "plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/lib/plan_status.py", "plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md", "tests/test_critic_gate_fallthrough.py", "tests/test_session_critic_gate.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py", "tests/test_verify_links_review_id.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/verify-links-review-id.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "linked_reviews' new 'anchor resolves, base_tree missing' branch is untested, and the docstring still says a missing base_tree links to nothing", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. It broke because the anchor lookup moved ahead of the base_tree guard, and the old guard sentence was kept. Before this change, a fact whose base_tree is not a non-empty string returned []. Now `if not isinstance(base, str) or not base: return [anchor] if anchor is not None else []` returns the recorded anchor. That is reasonable, because an id match is not the 'missing tree matches another missing tree' hazard the guard was written for. But no test covers it: every fixture in tests/test_verify_links_review_id.py has a valid base_tree. The docstring's closing sentence ('A base_tree that is not a non-empty string links to nothing (a missing tree must not match another fact's missing tree)') now says the opposite for an anchored pass. A maintainer who trusts that sentence could 'restore' the early return and nothing would fail. Rated WARNING, not BLOCKING: no validated writer reaches this branch (validate_manifest requires base_tree, and verify dispatch sets it to the prior's head_tree), so only a malformed or ingested fact can. Fix: add one parametrized case to TestTheLinkFollowsTheRecordedAnchor (base_tree None/'' with verifies naming a stored review -> [that review]; without verifies -> []). Make the docstring sentence relational: 'on the tree link, a base_tree that is not a non-empty string links to nothing'.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py", "tests/test_verify_links_review_id.py"], "fid": "R-1"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 1, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "_verify_anchor_id still proxies a future pass's anchor as the newest fact at the path's nodes", "recommendation": "Not a walker from a recorded pass, so the change record's list of walkers is accurate. Its docstring's 'residual' paragraph says a proper fix means giving the anchor a home in the shared store. This change gives a recorded pass's anchor that home, but not a future pass's, so the residual still stands as described. No edit wanted. Noted so nobody later reads `verifies` as having closed it.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Governing-Artifact Reconciliation: nothing to reconcile", "recommendation": "No plan claims fix/verify-links-review-id (manifest scope unbound), and the change record carries no governed_by dispositions, so there is no recorded disposition to test against the diff. record_lint's governed-by-gap count is 0.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/verify-links-review-id.md"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "Walk termination moved from the link rule's owner to each walker, and the new guards use a different identity than the existing one", "recommendation": "Before this change, strictly-before store order inside coverage_algebra.linked_reviews was what ended every walk. A recorded anchor is now found by id anywhere in the store, so termination is a caller obligation, written three times: gates._review_verified_passes_stand_on (new, id() object identity), plan_status._extended_reviews (new, id() object identity), and critic_mode.review_chain (existing, fact-id strings). linked_reviews' own docstring lists 'identity by id() vs by fact id' as one of the drifts that justified a single owner. A cycle needs a malformed store, because the producer picks the anchor from reviews that already exist and mints the pass id fresh, so no failure is reachable today. Scope: class. Closure: every loop that iterates prior_review/linked_reviews. Members: the three walkers named above. prior_review's docstring says nothing about the guard, so a fourth walker written against it could spin the Stop hook on a malformed ingested store. If this is ever touched, close it by construction: a single coverage_algebra generator that walks the link and owns the revisit guard, which all three walkers call. No edit is wanted for this merge.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/lib/plan_status.py", "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The anchor fixes linked_reviews[-1], but the 'earlier reviews at the same tree' members are still joined by tree from any worktree", "recommendation": "With an anchor, linked_reviews returns [same-tree reviews recorded before the anchor] + [anchor]. Reviews after the anchor at that tree are now excluded, but earlier same-tree reviews are still joined by tree whatever their worktree or branch. So if worktree B's pass anchors to the newer of two reviews at one tree, critic_mode.review_chain still includes sibling A's older review there. That chain feeds boundary_review_on_chain, chain_certified_chunks and _open_blocker_on_chain. The cross-worktree confusion this change targets is closed for 'which review does the pass verify', the anchor being prior_review's answer, but only half-closed for chain membership. This predates the change (the tree link included both reviews), and I did not trace whether a sibling's earlier cumulative or chunk on the chain changes any verdict in practice. One possible fix is to also bound the earlier same-tree members by the anchor's actor, or to record that the asymmetry is intended. Not rated as a finding: it is pre-existing and its consequence is unverified.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py", "plugin/lib/critic_mode.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "A dangling `verifies` claim is silent: no reader can tell 'anchor named but not in this store' from 'no anchor exists'", "recommendation": "_recorded_anchor returns (True, None) for an id the store lacks, and every walker reads that as no link with no trace. The Stop hook then says 'no review it verifies is on record' and recommends a full `final`, where the real remedy would be ingesting the missing review's notes. This is close to unreachable today. The Stop hook only walks from this worktree's own latest pass, and begin_review takes the anchor from the store, which is append-only, so the anchor was present when the pass was recorded. If a store-rebuild or cross-clone path ever makes it reachable, give the Stop reason a separate line for the dangling case that names the missing id. Instance, not class. No edit is wanted now.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-5"}], "duration_seconds": 600, "scope": null, "scope_chosen_by": "none", "scope_unresolved_cause": "unbound", "scope_reason": "no live plan claims `fix/verify-links-review-id`", "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunks_declared": false, "chunks_evidence": {}, "base_reviewed": "ecd39ffbf786afb8069915758108afe00603ddfa", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/data-model.md", ".prawduct/changes/verify-links-review-id.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-cycle.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0, "late-requirement-record": 0}}, "span": "full", "bounded_from": null, "span_reason": "no-boundary-review", "dispatched_at": "2026-11-23T19:37:13Z"}}
